+- **Classification:** Source error (misprint; plausibly copied from the neighbouring 7/8 q₀²j₀). **Scope:** the paper's own results are unaffected: its d_L coefficients D_L⁰…D_L⁴ (A6) and d_A coefficients (A7), used for the Fisher-matrix forecasts, are correct in the flat case (sympy, main session and referee; if the printed D⁴ had been used, D_L⁴ would carry an extra +21q₀⁴/8). Anyone using (A2) directly (lookback-time/age fits) gets a z⁵ coefficient off by 21q₀⁴/8 (≈ −0.55[✓F3_D4_LCDM(decel)] at q₀ = +0.24[✓F3_D4_LCDM], i.e. flat ΛCDM Ω_m = 0.3[in✓F3_D4_LCDM], more than doubling it).
